WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.526 --> 00:00:17.887
you guys ready to stop accusing me of stealing your money?"

2
00:00:18.428 --> 00:00:19.268
Ryan asked.

3
00:00:20.069 --> 00:00:22.430
"Because I'm not going to stand here all day.

4
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:23.910
See you later."

5
00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:27.172
Without waiting for an answer, he skated off.

6
00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:33.252
He stopped about half a block away and went back to practicing skateboarding tricks on the sidewalk.

7
00:00:34.793 --> 00:00:37.174
"Well, that was a waste of time," Cole said.

8
00:00:38.115 --> 00:00:40.237
Maggie watched Ryan do a fancy flip.

9
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:44.159
"I still think he did it," she muttered.

10
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.321
Henry was thinking hard.

11
00:00:46.341 --> 00:00:51.624
"If Ryan took that money, there must be a way to prove it."

12
00:00:51.644 --> 00:00:52.885
"I know."

13
00:00:53.506 --> 00:00:54.706
Cole cracked his knuckles.

14
00:00:54.726 --> 00:00:56.588
"Ryan's a lot smaller than us.

15
00:00:57.944 --> 00:00:59.685
We could hold him down and Maggie could search him."

16
00:00:59.705 --> 00:01:01.807
"Great idea!"

17
00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:03.448
Maggie's eyes lit up.

18
00:01:03.468 --> 00:01:05.329
"Let's go get him!"

19
00:01:07.311 --> 00:01:08.211
"Hold on."

20
00:01:08.812 --> 00:01:11.954
Henry grabbed Maggie's arm before she could rush down the block.

21
00:01:11.974 --> 00:01:14.255
"We can't do that."

22
00:01:14.275 --> 00:01:15.777
"Why not?"

23
00:01:16.177 --> 00:01:16.797
Maggie said.

24
00:01:16.817 --> 00:01:18.618
"He took my money!"

25
00:01:19.519 --> 00:01:21.941
For a second it looked as if she were about to cry.

26
00:01:21.961 --> 00:01:26.304
"I need that money for horseback-riding lessons."

27
00:01:27.344 --> 00:01:31.025
"We don't know for sure that he's the thief," Henry reminded her.

28
00:01:31.045 --> 00:01:33.986
"And it's not fair to gang up on him.

29
00:01:34.606 --> 00:01:37.767
If he didn't take your money, we'll get in big trouble."

30
00:01:38.627 --> 00:01:39.427
Maggie sighed.

31
00:01:39.447 --> 00:01:43.308
"I'm starting to think this investigation isn't worth it.

32
00:01:44.109 --> 00:01:47.390
Maybe I should just go back to the lemonade stand and start over."

33
00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:49.430
Cole nodded.

34
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:53.371
"And maybe you should put a lock on your cashbox," he suggested.

35
00:01:53.391 --> 00:01:55.912
"Good idea," Maggie said.

36
00:01:56.792 --> 00:01:58.453
Henry couldn't believe his ears.

37
00:01:58.473 --> 00:02:02.476
"You mean you guys are ready to give up already?

38
00:02:02.897 --> 00:02:05.318
But we're only on our first suspect!"

39
00:02:06.239 --> 00:02:07.100
Maggie shrugged.

40
00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:11.423
"Like you said, the thief is never going to admit to it.

41
00:02:12.103 --> 00:02:13.124
So what's the point?"

42
00:02:13.904 --> 00:02:16.967
"There has to be a way to figure out what happened."

43
00:02:18.328 --> 00:02:19.929
Henry turned to look at Ryan.

44
00:02:20.769 --> 00:02:24.032
Ryan was still ignoring them and practicing his skateboard tricks.

45
00:02:25.376 --> 00:02:29.097
He did a couple of flips, and then jumped the skateboard off the sidewalk.

46
00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:31.138
Henry stared at the shorts.

47
00:02:32.138 --> 00:02:34.919
He could see the pockets open every time Ryan moved.

48
00:02:34.939 --> 00:02:42.040
"If Ryan did take the money, he must have stuck it in his pockets," he murmured.

49
00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.921
"There's nowhere else he could be holding it.

50
00:02:45.881 --> 00:02:49.762
And he probably didn't have time to hide it anywhere between then and now."

51
00:02:49.783 --> 00:02:50.883
"Good point."

52
00:02:51.323 --> 00:02:51.943
Cole nodded.

53
00:02:51.963 --> 00:02:55.144
"Does that mean you want to hold him down and search him after all?"

54
00:02:56.152 --> 00:02:58.553
"No. I have a better idea."

55
00:02:59.933 --> 00:03:03.674
Henry hurried off toward Ryan before Maggie and Cole could respond.

56
00:03:04.254 --> 00:03:06.575
Ryan stopped skating when he saw him coming.

57
00:03:06.595 --> 00:03:11.896
"Oh, it's you again," he said, not sounding very happy.

58
00:03:11.916 --> 00:03:13.317
"Don't worry.

59
00:03:14.257 --> 00:03:16.518
I'm not here to ask you any more questions."

60
00:03:17.478 --> 00:03:19.158
Henry smiled at the younger kid.

61
00:03:19.178 --> 00:03:22.959
"Actually I was just watching you skate.

62
00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.840
You've got some nice moves."

63
00:03:25.524 --> 00:03:26.424
"Thanks, dude."

64
00:03:26.824 --> 00:03:29.445
Ryan looked suspicious but a little proud too.

65
00:03:29.465 --> 00:03:32.906
"So can you do some of the harder tricks?"

66
00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:34.066
Henry asked.

67
00:03:34.086 --> 00:03:39.508
"I saw a kid from Oakview School do some awesome tricks last weekend."

68
00:03:40.848 --> 00:03:43.149
Maggie and Cole had caught up to him by now.

69
00:03:43.169 --> 00:03:46.310
"Who cares what tricks he can do?"

70
00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:47.450
Maggie muttered.

71
00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:51.631
"I can do tons of cool stuff," Ryan bragged.

72
00:03:52.491 --> 00:03:55.032
"Way more than anybody from Oakview."

73
00:03:56.152 --> 00:04:00.175
"I saw that kid do a handstand on his skateboard," Henry said.

74
00:04:00.195 --> 00:04:01.776
"Can you do that?"

75
00:04:01.796 --> 00:04:04.198
"Sure. Watch me."

76
00:04:05.639 --> 00:04:08.041
Ryan skated a short distance away from them.

77
00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:13.845
Then he turned around and headed back toward them, kicking off with one foot to build up speed.

78
00:04:13.865 --> 00:04:17.308
"Who cares if he can do a handstand?"

79
00:04:17.708 --> 00:04:18.369
Maggie said.

80
00:04:18.389 --> 00:04:21.111
"Shh." Henry hushed her.

81
00:04:21.451 --> 00:04:22.292
"Just watch."

82
00:04:23.136 --> 00:04:28.038
As he got closer, Ryan leaned down and grabbed the edges of the board with his hands.

83
00:04:28.778 --> 00:04:32.520
A second later, he was upside-down with his legs in the air.

84
00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:35.681
"Awesome!" Cole cheered, clapping.

85
00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:37.002
"You're really good."

86
00:04:37.022 --> 00:04:41.464
"Thanks." Ryan flipped back onto his feet and stood up.

87
00:04:42.684 --> 00:04:45.925
His face was red, and his pockets were turned inside out.

88
00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:50.447
"I think you lost the stuff that was in your pockets," Henry said.

89
00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:51.888
"I'll help you pick it up."

90
00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:53.640
Henry stepped forward.

91
00:04:54.501 --> 00:04:58.942
A little pile of stuff lay in the spot where Ryan had flipped himself upside down.

92
00:04:59.762 --> 00:05:04.303
There was a peppermint candy, a house key, and a couple of snail shells.

93
00:05:05.324 --> 00:05:08.085
Henry grabbed it all and handed it back to Ryan.

94
00:05:08.945 --> 00:05:11.806
Then he said good-bye and hurried off around the corner.

95
00:05:12.746 --> 00:05:13.746
His friends followed.

96
00:05:13.766 --> 00:05:15.587
"What was that all about?"

97
00:05:15.927 --> 00:05:16.667
Cole asked.

98
00:05:16.687 --> 00:05:18.508
"Don't you get it?"

99
00:05:19.008 --> 00:05:19.868
Henry smiled.

100
00:05:20.388 --> 00:05:23.170
"I just proved that Ryan isn't our thief.

101
00:05:24.151 --> 00:05:28.854
If he'd stolen Maggie's money, it would have fallen out of his pockets along with all that other

102
00:05:28.914 --> 00:05:31.475
stuff." Cole's eyes widened.

103
00:05:31.495 --> 00:05:33.577
"Whoa! You're right!"

104
00:05:34.237 --> 00:05:35.638
Maggie looked impressed too.

105
00:05:36.338 --> 00:05:37.619
But she didn't look happy.

106
00:05:37.639 --> 00:05:39.721
"So now what?"

107
00:05:39.881 --> 00:05:40.461
she said.

108
00:05:40.741 --> 00:05:44.083
"If Ryan didn't take my money, then who did?"
